\subsection{Bidirectional Adaptation Transition}
\label{sec:roundtrip-transition-ablation}

The transition study presented in this article is a low--high--low non-stationary
record. The low-sea realization is
$(H_s,T_p)=(\SI{1.5}{m},\SI{5.7}{s})$. A $C^2$ quintic crossfade to the
high-sea realization $(\SI{4.0}{m},\SI{11.4}{s})$ begins at $t=400$~s and
ends at $t=520$~s. The high sea is held until $t=800$~s, when an identical
\SI{120}{s} crossfade returns to the \emph{same phase-randomized low-sea
realization}, ending at $t=920$~s. The high realization is randomized
independently. Velocity and acceleration retain the exact first- and
second-derivative blend terms, so the synthetic record remains kinematically
closed through both transitions.

\IfFileExists{ou_rs_roundtrip_transition.svg}{%
  \begin{figure}[t]
    \centering
    \includesvg[width=\columnwidth,inkscapelatex=false]{ou_rs_roundtrip_transition}
    \caption{OU--III Adaptive on the bidirectional low--high--low realization
    (wave, IMU and initialization seeds $11/101/1009$). Top: rolling
    \SI{60}{s} significant height and the mixture height implied by the
    quintic weights. Second: reference and estimated vertical displacement.
    Third: vertical error. Bottom: applied $\tau$, $\sigma_{aw}$ and $r_S$
    against the two frozen endpoint operating points. The shaded intervals are
    the rising and falling \SI{120}{s} $C^2$ crossfades; the dash-dotted line
    opens the scored \SI{900}{s} window.}
    \label{fig:ou-rs-roundtrip-protocol}
  \end{figure}
}{}

The scored \SI{900}{s} window is partitioned as
\emph{low-start} (300--400~s), \emph{rise} (400--520~s),
\emph{high-recovery} (520--640~s), \emph{high} (640--800~s),
\emph{fall} (800--920~s), \emph{low-recovery} (920--1040~s), and
\emph{low-return} (1040--1200~s). The complete segment scores are reported,
with the rise and fall crossfade scores kept separate so opposite-direction
adaptation lag cannot cancel in a pooled transition number.

\IfFileExists{w3d-roundtrip-transition-scores-generated.tex-part}{%
  \input{w3d-roundtrip-transition-scores-generated.tex-part}%
}{}

This protocol tests only the deployed SpectralMSE configuration. No historical
regularizer law is an arm of the transition study, and no one-way-transition
chart or score is used in the article.
